<title>GERMANY: German winter grain plantings seen up four pct.</title>
<headline>German winter grain plantings seen up four pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>German winter grain sowings for the 1997 harvest may rise by four percent from last year to 5.35 million hectares, the Bonn farm ministry said on Friday.</p>
<p>The ministry cited a survey of planting intentions and stressed the figures were preliminary.</p>
<p>Winter wheat and barley plantings were seen increasing four percent to 2.65 million and 1.48 million ha respectively.</p>
<p>Rye plantings were seen down four percent at 780,000 ha and triticale up around 25 percent at 450,000 ha.</p>
<p>Most winter grain is already in the ground.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
